{
  "subtype": "predictive_feature_engineering",
  "focus_variable": "state_declined",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "missing_source_id",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "A structural/metadata flag on the request that lies outside the outcome; missing source references could plausibly correlate with declines without restating the outcome."
    },
    {
      "name": "no_processed_date",
      "role": "leakage",
      "rationale": "processed_date reflects post-decision processing; whether a request was processed is largely determined by/coincident with its final disposition. Declined items may never be processed, making this a proxy for the outcome rather than an antecedent signal."
    },
    {
      "name": "amount_above_travel_median",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "A pre-decision property of the expense amount relative to the travel population; higher amounts plausibly carry predictive signal about declines and are knowable before the outcome."
    },
    {
      "name": "amount_below_dept_median",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "Another pre-decision amount-relative feature (vs department norm); legitimate antecedent signal, though partially redundant with the travel-median flag."
    },
    {
      "name": "user_prior_decline_rate",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "Historical decline rate of the user computed from PRIOR requests is a classic legitimate predictor, provided it excludes the current record. Strong signal, low leakage if computed correctly."
    },
    {
      "name": "high_decline_dept",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "Department-level historical decline propensity is a legitimate group-level predictor knowable before the outcome, assuming it is an aggregate not derived from the current row."
    },
    {
      "name": "submitted_off_hours",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "Submission timing derived from opened_at is a pre-decision behavioral feature that could plausibly carry weak predictive signal."
    },
    {
      "name": "decline_risk_score",
      "role": "leakage",
      "rationale": "A composite 'decline risk score' is a constructed estimate of the very outcome being predicted; if built to track state_declined it restates/leaks the target rather than providing an independent feature, and its heavy 0 mass mirrors the class split."
    }
  ],
  "n_predictors": 6,
  "predictive_utility": 0.6,
  "rationale": "As a set, most columns are legitimate antecedent features: amount-relative flags, user- and department-level historical decline propensities, submission-timing, and a metadata completeness flag give genuine predictive leverage beyond the raw columns, with the user/department history features being the strongest. However, two columns are problematic: no_processed_date effectively proxies whether the item reached processing, which is entangled with the final disposition, and decline_risk_score is a constructed estimate of the target itself (restatement/leakage). The predictor set also carries some internal redundancy (two amount-median flags, user vs dept history). Net: moderate, real predictive utility tempered by leakage in two columns."
}

